{"type":"text","timestamp":1794529562064,"sessionID":"ses_e2db8016dffezkR2BwTBxjhrBS","part":{"id":"prt_1d24bfcfd001G0a35yKjKEjCWt","sessionID":"ses_e2db8016dffezkR2BwTBxjhrBS","messageID":"msg_1d24bef5f001ynL5bbmT0kCC9F","type":"text","text":"T022 is implemented and verified.\n\n## Files written\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs`\n  - `project()` now computes the largest `runs` per arm across runtimes and sets `armIncomplete` on every arm block (`true` when the block's `runs` is below that arm's largest, else `false`). The `unscored` counter is skipped.\n  - `writeSummary()` appends `, arm incomplete` to the arm's text line when the flag is true.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`\n  - Added `runtime?: string` to the `RunLogLine` fixture shape and a `loadableCodexSession()` fixture using a real `session_meta` rollout.\n  - Added one case: claude runs 2, codex runs 1 in arm `tune`, asserting `claude.tune.armIncomplete === false` and `codex.tune.armIncomplete === true`.\n\n## Verify output\n\n`VT` (`npx vitest run tests/command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` in `ADV`):\n\n```\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  49 passed (49)\n```\n\nAttribution command:\n\n```\n$ node $S --summary $PRE --json | jq -c '[to_entries[] | select(.value.pre.armIncomplete == true) | .key]'\n[]\npipeline_exit=0\n```\n\nThe result is empty because all six runtimes in `$PRE` (`claude`, `codex`, `pi`, `devin`, `opencode`, `dsh`) have exactly 24 `pre` runs, so no runtime is below the arm's largest. Two supporting checks:\n\n- On a temp copy of `$PRE` with `dsh` reduced to 23 lines, the same command printed `[\"dsh\"]`, so the flag flips on real data.\n- The text line ends with `, arm incomplete` for the short runtime and without it for the complete one (verified on a temp log).\n\n## Notes\n\n- `$SP/summary-before.json` does not exist (the phase folder is untracked and only `.gitkeep`, logs and briefs are present), so I could not cross-check the per-runtime counts against it. The underlying `$PRE` counts were used directly.\n- I did not tick the `T022` checkbox and did not touch any other file.","time":{"start":1794529557757,"end":1794529562064}}}
